---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE, INFO_ROUTES, CATEGORIES, infoAlternates } from '@lib/site';
import { categoryHref } from '@lib/articles';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: 'About Yuuvi',
  url: new URL(INFO_ROUTES.about.en, Astro.site).toString(),
  inLanguage: 'en-US',
  isPartOf: {
    '@type': 'WebSite',
    name: SITE.name,
    url: new URL('/en/', Astro.site).toString(),
  },
};
---

<Layout
  title="About Yuuvi | Who we are"
  description="Yuuvi is an independent digital magazine about internet culture, trends, gaming, tech, style and music for the younger generation."
  lang="en"
  alternates={infoAlternates('about')}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="prose prose-invert prose-lg mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 prose-headings:font-black prose-headings:text-white prose-a:text-brand-pink [&_p]:text-neutral-300">
    <h1>About Yuuvi</h1>

    <p>
      <strong>Yuuvi is an independent digital magazine about internet culture and the trends shaping the
      younger generation.</strong> We explain what people share, argue about and turn into a trend online,
      with enough context to understand it even if you never watched the video everyone is talking about.
    </p>

    <h2>What Yuuvi is</h2>
    <p>
      We are not a general news site. We focus on one territory: the memes and slang born on TikTok, the
      aesthetics that come around every season, the games worth your time, the apps and gadgets people
      actually use, and the music that plays before it reaches the headlines.
    </p>
    <p>
      The idea is simple: if people are talking about it online, we want to explain where it comes from,
      how it is used and what is behind it. No posturing, no filler, no assuming the reader already knows.
    </p>

    <h2>What we cover</h2>
    <ul>
      {Object.entries(CATEGORIES).map(([slug, meta]) => (
        <li>
          <a href={categoryHref(slug, 'en')}><strong>{meta.label.en}</strong></a>: {meta.intro.en}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <h2>How we work</h2>
    <p>
      We choose topics for genuine interest, not search volume. When we publish a date, a name or a
      figure, we try to check it against a primary source and link to it whenever one is available. If we
      have tested an app, a game or a gadget, we say so; if we have not, we say that too.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every article shows its publication date and the person who wrote it. When a trend changes or a fact
      goes out of date, we revise the piece instead of letting it gather dust. And when we get something
      wrong, we correct it: you can always let us know from the contact page.
    </p>

    <h2>Independence and advertising</h2>
    <p>
      Yuuvi is funded by display advertising through Google AdSense. Ads do not influence which topics we
      cover or the opinions in our articles. If we ever publish sponsored content, it will be clearly
      labelled. We do not sell mentions, reviews or places in our rankings.
    </p>

    <h2>Who writes</h2>
    <p>
      Articles are signed by the <strong>Yuuvi Editorial</strong>, led by
      <strong>Pablo García Valentín</strong>. Every byline has its own page with that person&rsquo;s
      speciality and background. You can reach those pages from any article or from the author listings.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For suggestions, corrections, press or collaborations, email us at
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>. You will find the details on the
      <a href={INFO_ROUTES.contact.en}>contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
